bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:currentRecord bcoc:record-f32f3c25461cb2b3adf8eb70dcc8bd02a746e2eed40c9d53a14866e9bab9897d .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:definitionGenus cco:ont00000568 .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:lifecycleStatus "Draft" .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-3c7c642f5a0179876a5d092352483f454291c7d88136fc6870216096fdac53bc .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-7fbc3e395fbf7b5de65a40d2ae8efb38bd86a1bbd43695fb0d7bf146cb9ae03a .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance bco:sourceReference bcoc:source-aa18f2be9785bc5958d0fc79b9b3d3c15742ece3e290f43d0435a829edd67a81 .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance dcterms:created "2026-10-24T12:14:15+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance prov:wasAttributedTo bcoa:claude-opus-5-5 .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance rdf:type skos:Concept .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance skos:changeNote "2026-10-24, review R6 section 3.1: generalized, and the development clause removed. The definition said that acts first establishing this oversight develop the capability and are not, on that ground alone, realizations of it. That is specification CD5's distinction between developing and realizing a capability, and it is stated there for every capability; restating it in one definition made it read as a condition peculiar to this one. The definition now says what the capability is for. \"Realized in\" became \"realizable in\" (CD8). Every source is now marked contextual (R6 section 6.1)."@en .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance skos:definition "A business capability, inhering in an organization, that is realizable in planned acts by which that organization judges whether the business models it operates by still serve it, and decides how they should change."@en .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance skos:inScheme bcoc:CapabilityCatalogScheme .
bcoc:BusinessModelGovernance skos:prefLabel "Business Model Governance"@en .

